  "caption": "Quinn's touch footy debut ended with a dive straight onto the ball, ribs first. By the next day, every sneeze was a full event.\n\nBruised or cracked, the plan is often the same: keep breathing deeply and keep gently moving. Pain often eases over a few weeks, with twinges that can hang around longer.\n\nWhat often helps: slow deep breaths a few times an hour, hugging a pillow to cough, regular gentle walks, and sleeping propped up. Tight rib belts can keep breathing shallow, and heavy lifting and contact sport are best left until pain has well settled. Chat with your GP about pain relief.\n\nIncreasing breathlessness, chest pain that feels different, coughing blood, fever or dizziness need urgent medical care.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
